Subject: [PATCH] libzmq: bind ZAP, messages and monitors to a stream lifetime

Copyright 2026 RDK Management

Patch contents follow the licenses and linking exception of the affected
libzmq component. Existing licensing notices are preserved in the diff.

Base: upstream libzmq 4.3.4 release archive
Upstream-Status: Pending

Allocate an immutable local connection ID before the stream handshake. Expose
it and the FD as local ZAP and received-message metadata; snapshot UDS peer
credentials and include the lifetime in version-2 ACCEPTED/DISCONNECTED events.
Keep version-1 monitoring and the ZAP/ZMTP wire frames unchanged.

Add the opt-in downstream ROUTER_EXPECTED_CONNECTION_ID draft option so a
reply cannot follow a reused routing ID to another connection. Native transport
metadata cannot be overwritten by ZAP reply or peer metadata.

This replaces, rather than stacks on, the credential-only disconnect patch.
Version-2 consumers must handle the documented value counts. Gateway must
consume the new binding and use the send guard; the patch alone does not
implement Gateway session cleanup. Enable draft APIs in the library build.

Includes a Linux CMake regression test and integration documentation.

